What is a Coolant Distribution Unit (CDU)?
A Coolant Distribution Unit (CDU) is a critical component in modern liquid cooling systems for data centers, specifically engineered to regulate and distribute coolant with high precision across server racks. These sophisticated systems maintain optimal operating temperatures while dramatically reducing energy consumption compared to conventional cooling methods. CDUs typically incorporate pumps, heat exchangers, sophisticated control boards, and comprehensive monitoring devices that work in concert to manage coolant flow rates and system pressure. With data centers increasingly embracing liquid cooling to handle high-density computing environments, CDUs have become indispensable infrastructure elements supporting next-generation data processing capabilities.

Modern CDUs are designed to support rack power densities that now routinely exceed 20kW, with some hyperscale AI deployments pushing beyond 50kW. These thermal loads make liquid cooling through CDUs not just advantageous but essential, as liquid offers approximately 3,000 times greater heat transfer efficiency than air. Leading industry players such as Vertiv, Schneider Electric, and nVent are significantly expanding their CDU product portfolios to capitalize on this trend, particularly in the Asia-Pacific region where rapid data center construction in markets like China and India is driving unprecedented market expansion.

